      "id": 126078,
      "name": "Oaktree",
      "username": "Oaktree",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-11T19:04:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Most IL games are pretty short too.&nbsp; But I've seen two long ones:</p><p>1. Nightmist as surviving hero in Mist Form - she accumulated cards while incap hero powers took out on-goings and helped her draw more cards.&nbsp; Would drop out of Mist Form eventually to do a Mist-Fueled Recovery for HP, fight for a bit, and then go back to Mist Form if necessary.&nbsp;</p><p>2.&nbsp; Hero group included Legacy - and he got Next Evolution into play early as well as Lead From the Front.&nbsp; So he sat and tanked melee damage while the other heroes got time to do the work of taking IL down.</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:00:25.167Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
