      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-11T21:02:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Oaktree\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/48/2287_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Oaktree:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Most IL games are pretty short too.&nbsp; But I've seen two long ones:1. Nightmist as surviving hero in Mist Form - she accumulated cards while incap hero powers took out on-goings and helped her draw more cards.&nbsp; Would drop out of Mist Form eventually to do a Mist-Fueled Recovery for HP, fight for a bit, and then go back to Mist Form if necessary.&nbsp;2.&nbsp; Hero group included Legacy - and he got Next Evolution into play early as well as Lead From the Front.&nbsp; So he sat and tanked melee damage while the other heroes got time to do the work of taking IL down.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There is a third option for extended games and it is essential in the \"Easy way to beat IL\" method.</p>\n<p>Abuse IR's inability to destroy environments by hiding behind the Metor Storm in Wagner Mars Base.</p>\n<p>Do that with Golem Unity and have fun.</p>",
